body:
Band B3 (rusty-engine). PH-305b parity: implement the HF GPT-2/Qwen2 pre-tokenizer regex in std (no `regex` dep) — `gpt2_pre_split(text)->Vec<String>` with alternation: contractions ('s 't 're 've 'm 'll 'd) | [^
 L N]?L+ | N{1,3} | ?[^\s L N]+[
]* | \s*[
]+ | \s+(?!\S) | \s+. Use char::is_alphabetic (~\p{L}) / is_numeric (~\p{N}). Wire Bpe::encode to split ORIGINAL text via gpt2_pre_split per non-special segment, then bytes_to_chars + merge + byte-fallback (replacing the SPACE_MARK-only pre_tokenize). Tests: canonical GPT-2 splits ("Hello, world!" -> ["Hello",","," world","!"], contractions, digit runs N{1,3}, newline groups, trailing-space lookahead). No regressions in bpe_* round-trips. Gate fmt/clippy -D 0/test green. One local commit; no push.
